          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:08d182acfd692a1eebef1071cc3f9ede083618239bab4f9afad6fc7028389bc9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5946b80b745a4c2992414070b9062cdc",
      "statement": "AI-assisted coding (Claude Code) runs on the Claude MAX subscription. `MCM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is mapped to `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` only at the point of use in three separate processes (`agent-stack.mjs`, `wiki-maintain.mjs`, containerized E2E). Setting `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in any environment silently bills pay-per-token; this was measured at ~$15 unintended spend in one day (2026-08-16).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L5-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:703b6a465ca92025af8b9c1149149b8a0966d253c67c57b2e88766cc6b0bb583:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L14-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:077ac17be49b6aa5ab05589e9ef145c370fec61c1b0c2d45a33bdb74d5bee1bf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_baf437ba5f454f9881eb6f6f4871a115",
      "statement": "Before writing implementation code under `backend/`, `frontend/`, `agents/`, `mcp-servers/`, or `infrastructure-as-code/`, a numbered `specs/NNN-*/` spec → plan → tasks set must already exist. Proposals and knowledge/index edits are exempt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L6-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b0469b25fbc47f5514e0e5cd6fd4964fe1736c1c67f243ab1a9d80689c6ff51f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_92efebf75d9f4acfa0e4cd8f1644977d",
      "statement": "A PR's head must be a real branch (`git push origin HEAD:<branch>`), not an AGit push (`HEAD:refs/for/main`). An AGit push yields a `refs/pull/N/head` head that Forgejo runs with NO Actions secrets — every `${{ secrets.* }}` is empty. This cost two sessions on issue #126.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L8-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67f97dd647965610c9495cf40f2271575e1b4f95287528ecf4d4a59142764001:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/ci-diagnostics.md#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eef041abc54fd0632ab73a5265310803d82c913bc8e227fc5cfaf08b2eaae194:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a96549b5bd8b4245964101e60ee837bd",
      "statement": "`sbx start` is not a valid command — it silently prints the root help. To restart a stopped sandbox, use `sbx run --name mcm -d`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L90-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:630b0b241cca7080e7d1517b1f867a03b1e8072d034fda7f67d3f8d2297460b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59d86e031a974bd98950cae7297be71e",
      "statement": "`--name` is load-bearing on `sbx run` because the first positional argument is an agent, not a sandbox name. Omitting it can create a second sandbox instead of restarting the existing one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L95-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab85603430843b4f145e9c7f4192039d772575f572ea39140b20439367aa7e1a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b607f6b0b54e434483c2aff7b3b6d941",
      "statement": "`sandboxd` does not auto-start at boot. `sbx run --name mcm -d` starts it on demand. Reaching for `ssh mcm.sbx` before starting it surfaces a daemon error that reads like a broken environment rather than a cold host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L99-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e752daebd812b8a07c8547d2b1afc3d956ba91a9aa50e2e668e511a0cdbb6e95:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea4d53b90dee4893a3e4a8838f08e294",
      "statement": "`sbx template save` snapshots the VM root filesystem, not the Docker data disk, so a sandbox recreated from a template starts with zero images. The egress policy is also not carried in a template — a recreated sandbox gets the default profile and must have its policy re-applied.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:276c5cdeab693441ce0ff737154f9892d269fbd1cf0af75a8efd1dd1b85df16e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_51ac2a450acc4ebab5ed02fc22c081e0",
      "statement": "`sbx run` mounts the current directory as the sandbox workspace over virtiofs, read-write, unless an explicit path is given. Creating a sandbox from inside the repo mounts the repo into the VM. Measured 2026-08-16: a file written inside a recreated sandbox appeared immediately in the Windows working copy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:276c5cdeab693441ce0ff737154f9892d269fbd1cf0af75a8efd1dd1b85df16e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_270348d6b84f4852bd110ae49e627305",
      "statement": "The `docker-outside-of-docker` feature fronts the VM socket with a socat relay whose half-close timeout defaults to 0.5 s. `docker exec` half-closes stdin immediately, so socat tears the relay down mid-response — fast commands return exit 0 with no output. The fix is to use `DOCKER_HOST=unix:///var/run/docker-host.sock`, already applied in `.devcontainer/sandbox/devcontainer.json`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L180-L226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17909d7a44db470dde622d4ba8d2d40794fcfef4d12e427d3f0577d781650051:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1336a6cd9d764aa0a75fca600b5b7d46",
      "statement": "In the sandbox, the in-VM firewall (`ipset`/`iptables`) is not used; enforcement is the host-side policy outside the VM. Egress triage order is therefore host policy first, in-VM second — the opposite of the Docker Desktop path. `nc -z <ip> 443` reports OPEN against a blocked destination because the proxy accepts TCP and refuses at TLS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L185-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:821f8d9988e92280b5bcb7091e8777c9cc8b8dcc55796fe01aedb371b5439873:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7c0a0fc6da6473c82edbb1d1d65d7e7",
      "statement": "Git must run inside the dev container, not in the VM shell. The VM user and container user previously had different UIDs (uid 1000 vs a different uid), causing git writes from the VM shell to be unwritable by the container user. Fixed 2026-08-17: `toolchain.Dockerfile` now creates `coder` at 1000:1000.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:276c5cdeab693441ce0ff737154f9892d269fbd1cf0af75a8efd1dd1b85df16e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_58ba995640414751b0850e3a4e0a7274",
      "statement": "Every `containerEnv` entry in a devcontainer.json becomes an `ENV` instruction in the generated derived image, making it permanently readable in `Config.Env` and history layers. Measured on the derived image on 2026-09-19: all four credential values were present in `Config.Env` and in three history layers. Credentials must go through the runtime env file written by `.devcontainer/gen-container-secrets-env.sh`, not declared in `containerEnv`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L141-L141",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3679ee6b341a7fcbf81c7e6cd5b32a4eeca4af2aafed9163193d6fbbac62c18:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer-sandbox.md#L127-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fbbdef1ca33aecc582a2af7d209114e50bfda178045a406671b8af13e30dddc8:"
        }
      ]
    }
